Package: ogeom
Type: Package
Title: Nonlinear Regression on Sparsely Observed Gaussian Curves
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: person("Ufuk", "Beyaztas", email = "ufuk.beyaztas@marmara.edu.tr",
    role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: Implements Galerkin chaos estimators for binary regression on a
    Gaussian trajectory that is measured at a few irregular times per subject.
    The package computes the exact conditional features and the information
    operators of a sampling design, which show which nonlinear effects of the
    trajectory the design can identify, and fits the estimators with an
    unbiased risk criterion for the truncation level. Data-generating functions
    reproduce the simulation designs of the accompanying paper, including
    Brownian motion measured once at a uniformly distributed time.
License: GPL (>= 3)
Encoding: UTF-8
Depends: R (>= 3.5.0)
Imports: stats
Suggests: fdapace
NeedsCompilation: no
